my mail, I will probably start filtering extropians based on poster
reputation. Messages from folks with bad reps will end up in my 
"to-be-read-someday" folder. Messages from people with better reps will
bubble to the top.

I don't know all the ways in which it could be used, but I suspect that
they will develop once we have the mechanism for measuring reputation.

> I understand that markets need not trade in tangibles, that markets can
> take on a reality unto themselves (as in the Dutch tulip bulb speculative
> bubble), but this market seems generally uninteresting.

I initiated this as a response to the suggestion that was made for a 
central bank/betting system and to all of the "societies" that were
being proposed. In all of these, complex procedures were required. The
betting system was the worse, as it required people to keep track
of which messages they had read, and spend a large amount of time
evaluating them.

I wanted to come up with some way of achieving the same sorts of goals
without an onerous amout of work. With the reputation market, you don't
have to track individual messages. If you like something someone posted,
fire off a buy order. If they start spouting nonsense, fire off a sell
order.

Of course, if you are uninterested in the problem of measuring peoples
reactions to you in the sort of environment we have on Extropians, it
makes sense that you would find this market uninteresting.

